[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known, with one issue and one fix queued. Its reports describe
three problems, and the queued fix addresses one of them.

<Callout>
Do not close #4471 when the parser fix ships. The other two problems will still be open.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

- **`parser`:** the shared parser reads every date month first, so tenants that write the day first
  get the day and month swapped. This is the bug the queued fix is for.
- **`hint`:** booking-v3's form tells people to type `MM/DD/YYYY`, then reads what they type the
  tenant's way. Only reports through that form belong here. The same tenants' app and email reports
  are `parser`.
- **`one-day shift`:** these reports describe a booking off by one day, or different days for
  different people, and not a swap. A time zone bug is the likely lead, but it is not confirmed.

## How the reports were counted

Each report is placed by its tenant and way in, using `causes.ts`, and repeated export rows count
once. Intake's tag was not used, because it follows the reporter's browser and not the tenant.

The cause table on the #4471 page has no third row. It files the one-day reports under `parser` by
tenant, as the desk notes say, so its `parser` count includes them. The table above takes them out
because their symptom is different. If the investigation shows they are swaps, they go back.

## How they came to be merged

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports on subject line alone, and
reporters describe all three problems with the same few subjects. The rule accepts that one bug may
get several tickets. It did not consider one ticket hiding several bugs.

## What the desk should do

- Ship the parser fix, then keep the other two tickets open until each has its own fix.
- Reply to the booking-v3 tenants that the parser fix will not cover their form.
- Write a new decision record to replace 0001, one that merges on cause. The
  [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) follows 0001 and would change with it.

